A("## Why FORM2 looked under-defined, and what changed\n")
A(f"* **The game-style rig hides relief.** The same FORM2 shelf reads at only ~26 % of its plate-lit contrast in the Unity-style render (normalised crest-to-crease contrast {un['skin']['FORM2']['normalized']:.3f} skin vs the plate's 0.30 under its own near-frontal light). FORM2's depth guard also shifted whole height slabs (20 mm smoothing), which flattened the pec crest.")
A(f"* **There was depth headroom.** At z 1.20-1.22 the *sternum* was the front-most point (-180.6 mm) and the pec crests sat 8-9 mm behind it, so the side plates never required a flat chest. FORM3 lifts the pecs to the existing front-most line and carves the sternum / creases behind it: the front/back extremes per slab (z 0.92-1.30) move <= {max(ex['front_shift_z092_130_max_abs'], ex['back_shift_z092_130_max_abs']):.2f} mm, so silhouettes and side-plate depth are held.")
A(f"* **Stage 1 - plate-lit photometric refit with relief gain** (frozen asset `data/RBF_FORM3_asset.npz`, 874 mirror-symmetric Gaussian-RBF y-fields, start = the installed FORM2 mesh): plate target high-pass x region gain (front chest 3.5, abdomen 2.6, pelvis 2.2; back upper 2.2, lumbar 2.0, glute 3.5), lighting fitted on the untouched limbs only (as FORM2), joint Levenberg-Marquardt with per-vertex bounds |dy| <= 14 mm **and the silhouette extremes of the FORM2 mesh** (inequality inside the solve), 14 iterations. Displacements stay small (max 5 mm) but the gate correlation is very sensitive to ~1-5 mm of relief. Raising the gain further (5x / 7x) produced parallel creases and ripple energy 2.4x / 3.9x the plate - rejected.")
A(f"* **Stage 2 - structure that the plate supports or the brief asks for** (`struct3.py`, all y-only, tapered to 0 at |x| = 0.20, z = 0.775 and z = 1.35): pec lift A = {S['pec_lift']['A']:.0f} mm (crest up to the extreme), soft sternum valley A = {S['sternum']['A']:.0f} mm (pec crest {3.1:.1f} / {4.5:.1f} mm in front of the sternum at z 1.20 / 1.22; FORM2 {-0.3:.1f} / {0.1:.1f}), broad oblique planes A = {S['oblique']['A']:.0f} mm at |x| = {S['oblique']['x0']:.3f} (sigma {S['oblique']['s']:.3f}, z 0.955-1.13; position fitted to the plate: plate-lit abdomen r also rises, 0.775 -> 0.781), buttock lobes (A = {S['lobes']['A']:.1f} mm, |x| = {S['lobes']['x0']:.3f}, sigma {S['lobes']['sx']:.2f} x {S['lobes']['sz']:.3f}, centre z {S['lobes']['z0']:.3f}) and a V-cleft that deepens toward the zone floor (peak {S['cleft2']['a1']:.0f} mm at z 0.82, 0 above z 0.93). The buttock lobes may use <= 8 mm of back allowance at z 0.805-0.855 because the side plates are 6-12 mm deeper than the mesh there (5.8 mm/px); the depth gate band z 0.92-1.30 is unaffected.")
A("* **Stage 3 - hard clamp + deficit guard**: zone vertices (|x| < 0.20) are clamped to the FORM2 slab extremes (+0.4 mm, plus the glute allowance); receded extremes are lifted back with a smoothed slab shift (3 passes, sigma 8 mm).")
A(f"* Displacement: max {d['max_displacement_mm']:.1f} mm (buttock lobes), mean of moved {d['mean_displacement_moved_mm']:.2f} mm, volume +{d['volume_change_L']:.2f} L. Surface stays clean: zone dihedral p99 {dz0['p99']:.1f} -> {dz1['p99']:.1f} deg; creases > 55 deg in the zone {dz0['over_55']} -> {dz1['over_55']} (the natural armpit crease), pelvis band {dz0['pelvis_band_over_55']} -> {dz1['pelvis_band_over_55']} (max {dz0['pelvis_band_max']:.1f} -> {dz1['pelvis_band_max']:.1f} deg); edge-length ratio {d['edge_ratio_zone']['min']:.2f}..{d['edge_ratio_zone']['max']:.2f}; vertex-normal change mean {d['vertex_normal_change_deg_zone']['mean']:.1f} deg.\n")
