A(f"* **Held-out check is slightly WORSE.** The two back 3/4 panels of the sheet (validation only, never fitted; the AI plates are not fully 3D-consistent) correlate less with FORM3: left {ho['FORM2']['q3BL']:.3f} -> {ho['FORM3']['q3BL']:.3f}, right {ho['FORM2']['q3BR']:.3f} -> {ho['FORM3']['q3BR']:.3f}; glute band {ho['FORM2']['q3BL_glute']:.2f}/{ho['FORM2']['q3BR_glute']:.2f} -> {ho['FORM3']['q3BL_glute']:.2f}/{ho['FORM3']['q3BR_glute']:.2f}, lumbar {ho['FORM2']['q3BL_lumbar']:.2f}/{ho['FORM2']['q3BR_lumbar']:.2f} -> {ho['FORM3']['q3BL_lumbar']:.2f}/{ho['FORM3']['q3BR_lumbar']:.2f}, upper back {ho['FORM2']['q3BL_upper']:.2f}/{ho['FORM2']['q3BR_upper']:.2f} -> {ho['FORM3']['q3BL_upper']:.2f}/{ho['FORM3']['q3BR_upper']:.2f}. The frozen photometric fit alone moves the panels {ho['FORM2']['q3BL']:.3f} -> {ho['RBF_asset_only']['q3BL']:.3f} (left) and {ho['FORM2']['q3BR']:.3f} -> {ho['RBF_asset_only']['q3BR']:.3f} (right); the requested buttock lobes + cleft take them on to {ho['FORM3']['q3BL']:.3f} / {ho['FORM3']['q3BR']:.3f} (glute band {ho['RBF_asset_only']['q3BL_glute']:.2f}/{ho['RBF_asset_only']['q3BR_glute']:.2f} -> {ho['FORM3']['q3BL_glute']:.2f}/{ho['FORM3']['q3BR_glute']:.2f}, lumbar even improves {ho['RBF_asset_only']['q3BL_lumbar']:.2f}/{ho['RBF_asset_only']['q3BR_lumbar']:.2f} -> {ho['FORM3']['q3BL_lumbar']:.2f}/{ho['FORM3']['q3BR_lumbar']:.2f}) and the glute-band loss trades almost linearly against cleft depth (6 / 10 / 15 mm cleft: left glute band 0.82 / 0.79 / 0.72). The primary front/back plates improve in all six regions; the brief names the 3/4 panels as validation only, so this is disclosed rather than gated.")
A("* **The gate metric is lighting-capped and hypersensitive.** It compares a Unity-style render with a plate lit almost head-on; the same mesh Unity-lit vs plate-lit correlates only ~0.68, and ~1-5 mm of relief moves the band-passed r by 0.1-0.2 (the pec/abdomen/glute gains are real and visible, but absolute r is not 'fidelity'). The joint solver's path matters: running front and back as independent solves stalls on the back (stuck at a worse minimum), so the validated joint solution is frozen as an asset.")
A("* **Not fixed (belongs to other zones or resolution-limited).** The plate's gluteal fold arcs, thigh overhang and the squared crotch slot (z < 0.77, legs zone) - the cleft ends in a closing ramp at the zone floor; the plate's pecs are rounder and bigger in 3/4 than the silhouette-bound mesh allows; the shelf fades at the sternum (the plate's own centre dip is only ~4 lum); vertex spacing is ~11.5 mm with no vertex on the midline, so creases cannot get sharper than 2 vertices; the Unity-style shelf contrast ({:.0f} lum) is still below the plate's own normalised contrast because the rig is flatter.".format(un['skin']['FORM3']['drop_lum']))
A("* **Unity not refreshed.** The Unity project keeps its own FBX copy (`Unity/Assets/Characters/HeroBase/Models/`); other chats were still installing, so only the ArtDir blend + FBX were updated (`HeroBaseMaleFormProof.cs` `ExpectedTriangles` must be 66158 when it is refreshed).\n")
